                    <h3>Introduction</h3>
                    <p>This Domain Name Registration Agreement ("Agreement") is entered into between you, the individual or organization registering one or more domain names, and {$companyname} (referred to as "the Company," "we," or "us"), acting as the sponsoring registrar or reseller for the registry listed in the WHOIS record available publicly.</p>
                    <p>By using our domain registration services ("Services"), you confirm that you have read, understood, and agreed to be bound by this Agreement. We strongly recommend reviewing it carefully before proceeding with any domain registration, renewal, transfer, or related service.</p>
                    <p>This Agreement supplements our Terms of Service and Privacy Policy. In the event of any conflict between this Agreement and our Terms of Service, the terms most protective of the Company shall prevail with respect to domain-related matters.</p>

                    <h3>Definitions</h3>
                    <p><strong>"Registrant"</strong> means the individual or entity identified in the WHOIS database as the registered holder of a domain name.</p>
                    <p><strong>"Registry"</strong> means the organization responsible for maintaining the master database of domain names for a specific top-level domain (TLD).</p>
                    <p><strong>"Registrar"</strong> means an entity accredited by ICANN or a ccTLD authority to register domain names on behalf of Registrants.</p>
                    <p><strong>"WHOIS"</strong> means the publicly queryable database containing contact and technical information associated with registered domain names.</p>
                    <p><strong>"UDRP"</strong> means the Uniform Domain Name Dispute Resolution Policy established by ICANN for resolving disputes regarding domain name registrations.</p>
                    <p><strong>"gTLD"</strong> refers to generic top-level domains (e.g., .com, .net, .org, .info), while <strong>"ccTLD"</strong> refers to country-code top-level domains (e.g., .us, .uk, .ca).</p>
                    <p><strong>"Privacy Protection"</strong> or <strong>"WHOIS Privacy"</strong> means the service that replaces Registrant contact information in the public WHOIS database with proxy contact details.</p>

                    <h3>Domain Registration Rules</h3>
                    <p>A domain registration becomes active only when all of the following conditions are met:</p>
                    <p>You accept this Agreement and our Terms of Service; {$companyname} approves your registration request at its sole discretion; applicable registration, renewal, or restoration fees have been successfully paid; and your domain details are submitted to the relevant registry and approved.</p>
                    <p>You may not register a domain name if you are prohibited from entering into binding contracts under applicable law. All domain registrations are subject to availability and registry acceptance. We reserve the right to reject any registration request at our discretion, including but not limited to requests that violate trademark rights, applicable laws, or ICANN policies.</p>
                    <p>In line with ICANN requirements, we reserve the right to reject or limit multiple domain registration requests at our discretion. The registration of a domain name does not confer any intellectual property rights, trademark rights, or other proprietary interests in the domain name to you.</p>
                    <p>Some domains are classified as premium due to their value or demand. Premium domain pricing may be corrected at any time, and orders may be adjusted or cancelled with full refund in the event of a pricing error. You are responsible for verifying pricing before completing any purchase.</p>

                    <h3>Registrant Responsibilities</h3>
                    <p>You must provide accurate, complete, and up-to-date registration details at all times, including: registrant name and contact information; domain name requested; administrative, technical, and billing contacts; and nameserver and DNS details.</p>
                    <p>You agree to update this information within seven (7) days of any changes. Failure to provide accurate or updated information may result in suspension, cancellation, or loss of your domain. {$companyname} may collect and store additional registration data including creation dates, renewal history, and technical logs as required by ICANN or applicable registry operators.</p>
                    <p>You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of any authentication credentials associated with your domain registration account. You must immediately notify us of any unauthorized access or suspected security breach.</p>
                    <p>You represent and warrant that: you have authority to enter into this Agreement; this Agreement is legally binding upon you; no conflicting legal obligations exist that would prevent your compliance; and all information provided is accurate, complete, and not misleading.</p>
                    <p>You are solely responsible for ensuring that your registration and use of any domain name does not infringe upon the intellectual property rights or other legal rights of any third party. We assume no responsibility for monitoring or enforcing such compliance.</p>

                    <h3>Payment & Renewal Policy</h3>
                    <p>All domain registration services require full payment before processing. Fees vary based on domain extension, registration period, and payment method. All payments are non-refundable unless otherwise required by applicable law. Fees may be changed with fourteen (14) days' advance notice published on our website.</p>
                    <p>Domains may be suspended or transferred in case of chargebacks, payment disputes, or fraudulent transactions. Services may be paused until outstanding fees are settled in full, including any applicable late fees or collection costs.</p>
                    <p>You are solely responsible for renewing your domain before expiration. Failure to renew may result in loss of ownership, deletion of the domain from the registry, and potential registration by a third party. Domains may enter expiration and redemption cycles, during which additional fees may apply to restore the domain.</p>
                    <p>Auto-renewal may be enabled using your selected payment method. You may opt out of auto-renewal at any time through your client portal, provided such opt-out is completed before the renewal date. {$companyname} is not liable for any loss resulting from failure to renew a domain name, including losses due to expired payment methods or failed auto-renewal attempts.</p>

                    <h3>Domain Transfers</h3>
                    <p>Domain transfers or ownership changes require approval from both current and new registrants. Transfers may be restricted within sixty (60) days of initial registration or a prior transfer, per ICANN policy, except in limited circumstances such as court orders or disputes.</p>
                    <p>We may act as designated agent for registrant changes when such changes are initiated through our platform. By initiating a transfer or ownership change, you authorize us to process such requests on your behalf, subject to applicable verification requirements.</p>
                    <p>Transfers may be denied in cases of fraud, dispute, policy violation, or outstanding fees. No refunds are issued after successful transfers. The gaining registrar may require additional verification steps, and you are responsible for responding to all transfer confirmation requests within the specified timeframes.</p>
                    <p>You must ensure that any domain to be transferred is not locked, does not have privacy protection services that would interfere with verification, and has up-to-date contact information to receive transfer authorization communications.</p>

                    <h3>Suspension & Termination</h3>
                    <p>This Agreement remains active until: the domain is cancelled by you; the domain is transferred to another registrar; or the domain expires without renewal. We may suspend or terminate domains for: policy violations; legal requirements; fraud or abuse; non-payment; or breach of any provision of this Agreement.</p>
                    <p>Upon suspension or termination, all associated services may be immediately discontinued. You remain liable for all fees incurred prior to termination. No refunds apply in cases of willful violations, fraud, or conduct that jeopardizes the security or integrity of our systems or the registry.</p>
                    <p>We may suspend privacy services in cases of abuse, fraud, legal requirement, or dispute resolution proceedings. Suspension does not relieve you of your obligation to pay all outstanding fees.</p>
                    <p>In the event of termination, you acknowledge that we have no obligation to retain your registration data beyond any period required by ICANN or applicable law. Certain provisions of this Agreement, including those relating to indemnification, liability limitations, and dispute resolution, shall survive termination.</p>

                    <h3>ICANN Compliance</h3>
                    <p>You agree to comply with all applicable ICANN policies, including but not limited to the Registration Accreditation Agreement (RAA), the WHOIS Accuracy Program Specification, and any interim policies or specifications adopted by ICANN from time to time. These policies are incorporated into this Agreement by reference.</p>
                    <p>By registering a domain, you authorize {$companyname} to share required registration data with ICANN, registry operators, and legal authorities when necessary. You waive any claims related to lawful disclosure of such information as required by ICANN policy or applicable law.</p>
                    <p>ICANN may conduct compliance audits, and you agree to cooperate fully with any such audit. We may be required to verify your contact information periodically, and you consent to receiving verification notices and responding to them within the specified timeframes.</p>
                    <p>If you fail to comply with ICANN-mandated verification requests, your domain may be suspended or cancelled in accordance with ICANN policy. We shall not be liable for any loss arising from such suspension or cancellation when undertaken to comply with ICANN requirements.</p>

                    <h3>Dispute Resolution (UDRP)</h3>
                    <p>You agree to comply with ICANN's Uniform Domain Name Dispute Resolution Policy (UDRP) and any applicable registry dispute procedures. The UDRP is incorporated into this Agreement by reference and is available at <a href="https://www.icann.org/resources/pages/help/dndr/udrp-en" target="_blank">www.icann.org</a>.</p>
                    <p>{$companyname} may suspend, lock, or transfer domains involved in disputes or legal proceedings at the direction of a court, arbitration panel, or approved dispute resolution provider. We are not a party to any dispute between you and a third party regarding domain ownership or use.</p>
                    <p>You agree to submit to the jurisdiction of the courts located in the jurisdiction of our principal place of business for the resolution of any dispute not subject to the UDRP or other mandatory dispute resolution policy. You further agree that any legal action arising from this Agreement shall be governed by the laws of that jurisdiction, without regard to conflict of law principles.</p>
                    <p>In the event of a dispute, you agree to hold {$companyname} harmless from any claims, losses, or damages arising from our compliance with dispute resolution decisions, court orders, or requests from law enforcement authorities.</p>

                    <h3>Limitation of Liability</h3>
                    <p>{$companyname}, its registry partners, service providers, and affiliates shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, punitive, or consequential damages arising from the use or inability to use our Services, even if advised of the possibility of such damages.</p>
                    <p>We are not responsible for losses resulting from: unauthorized access or misuse of authentication data; force majeure events including natural disasters, acts of government, or Internet failures; service interruptions or delays; data loss, corruption, or misdelivery; errors or inaccuracies in registration data; or service downtime or disruption.</p>
                    <p>In all cases, our maximum liability shall not exceed the total amount paid by you for the specific domain registration during the twelve (12) months preceding the event giving rise to liability. This limitation applies regardless of the form of action, whether in contract, tort, negligence, strict liability, or otherwise.</p>
                    <p>We provide all Services "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any kind, either express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. We do not warrant that the Services will be uninterrupted, timely, secure, or error-free.</p>

                    <h3>Modifications to Agreement</h3>
                    <p>We reserve the right to update, amend, or remove any part of this Agreement at any time. Where changes are made, a notice will be published on our website for at least thirty (30) days prior to the effective date of such changes. The revision date will be updated at the top of this document.</p>
                    <p>Continued use of our Services after changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the updated Agreement. If you do not agree to the modified terms, your sole remedy is to cancel your domain services and cease using our platform.</p>
                    <p>We may also modify this Agreement without advance notice where required to comply with ICANN policies, registry operator rules, court orders, or applicable law. Such modifications shall be effective immediately upon posting. Your continued use of the Services following any modification constitutes binding acceptance.</p>
                    <p>It is your responsibility to review this Agreement periodically. We are not obligated to notify you individually of changes, though we may choose to do so for significant modifications. The most current version of this Agreement will always be available on our website.</p>

